Updating Information for users of HalfBSD.

20261002:
	Direct PVH kernel boot and the Firecracker kernel configuration and
	release image targets have been removed.  Remove the PVH option from
	custom kernel configurations.  Firecracker guests are no longer
	supported; amd64 systems must boot through the UEFI loader.

20261002:
	The cal and ncal calendar-display commands and their libcalendar
	helper library have been removed from the base system.

20261002:
	The mlx4 core, Ethernet, and InfiniBand drivers have been removed.
	Remove mlx4, mlx4en, and mlx4ib devices from custom kernel
	configurations and their load directives from loader.conf.
	Mellanox adapters requiring these drivers are no longer supported.

20261002:
	Import the FreeBSD 15.1-RELEASE-p4 security and errata fixes:
	EN-26:23.syslogd, EN-26:24.tzdata, SA-26:64.sysvsem,
	SA-26:65.kqueue, SA-26:66.jail, SA-26:67.ktls,
	SA-26:68.openssl, and SA-26:69.udp.

	These fix syslogd pipe-child cleanup on reload, semaphore and kqueue
	memory-safety bugs, jail filesystem escapes, receive-side kernel TLS
	denial of service, OpenSSL DTLS retransmission, and IPv6 UDP jail
	network isolation.  The timezone database is updated to 2026d.

	The new kern.ipc.tls.rx_enable tunable allows TLS receive offload
	to be disabled independently of transmit offload.

20261001:
	The x86 BIOS boot loaders have been removed.  Systems must now boot
	using UEFI.  Before updating, install loader.efi in an EFI System
	Partition and confirm that the firmware is configured to use it.

20261001:
	The syscons rc service and devd configuration have been renamed to
	vtcons to reflect that they configure the vt(4) console.  Update local
	references from "service syscons" to "service vtcons".  New per-service
	configuration belongs in /etc/rc.conf.d/vtcons; the vtcons script
	temporarily loads /etc/rc.conf.d/syscons first for compatibility, with
	settings in /etc/rc.conf.d/vtcons taking precedence.
